course: dictionary
lesson: 1286
title: Buttermilk and clues from context
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Buttermilk sounds like milk with butter in it, but the context shows it is something left behind. «Shake cream in a jar long enough and the droplets stick together into butter, leaving buttermilk behind.» The clues are shake, cream, butter and leaving behind. So buttermilk is what remains after the butter is made.
explain: Look at the word «leaving». It tells you buttermilk is not the butter itself. It is the liquid that is still there once the fat has stuck together. When you meet a new word, ask: what is left over? That question is a clue.
explain: Another sentence adds more: «Whisk it gently instead and the fat holds air bubbles as whipped cream.» Here whisking gives a different result, whipped cream, not buttermilk. The context shows you that buttermilk comes from shaking, and that the same cream can end up in different forms.
fact: Buttermilk is the slightly sour liquid left after butter has been made from cream.
fact: Some buttermilk in shops is milk made sour and thick on purpose, and it is used in baking.
fact: Buttermilk is uncountable, so we say some buttermilk, not a buttermilk.
fact: Buttermilk helps pancakes, scones and soda bread become soft and fluffy.
fact: «About 20 litres of milk make one kilogram of butter» shows that butter takes a lot of milk to make.
exercise: «Shake cream in a jar long enough and the droplets stick together into butter, leaving buttermilk behind.» What is buttermilk in this sentence? | *What is left after the butter is made | Air bubbles in whipped cream | Cream that has not been shaken | The butter itself
exercise: Ella says buttermilk is just butter with milk in it. Which clue shows she is wrong? | The word whisk, because it makes butter | The word jar, because it is a container | *The word leaving, because buttermilk is what is left behind | The word cream, because it is butter
exercise: Mum bakes «buttermilk scones» for the school fair. What does buttermilk tell you about the scones? | *They are made with sour, thick milk liquid | They are eaten only at breakfast | They are served cold with whipped cream | They are made with melted butter only
test: «Whisk it gently instead and the fat holds air bubbles as whipped cream.» What does this sentence show? | Whipped cream is the same as buttermilk | *Whisking and shaking can make different results from the same cream | Cream cannot be changed at all | Whisking always makes butter
test: Which word means the sour liquid used in baking, sold in shops? | *Buttermilk | Butter | Whisk | Droplet
exam: In «buttermilk pancakes», what does buttermilk tell you? | A kind of cream that is never shaken | A shape for cooking the pancakes | A type of cheese | *An ingredient that makes the pancakes soft and fluffy
